cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kelvra: a policy language and audit format for information flow in LLM agent pipelines"
message: "If you refer to Kelvra in academic work, please cite it as below. Note that it is early-stage and the label model is unstable."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "SAWADOGO"
    given-names: "Azaël Wend-panga"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NICE-DEV226/kelvra"
abstract: >-
  Kelvra specifies a label model and provenance format for information flow
  control in LLM agent pipelines. Labels carry three axes -- confidentiality,
  integrity and purpose -- joined by intersection, with relaxation permitted
  only through explicitly declared declassification. A model call is treated
  as a total join over its inputs, which is coarse but never under-labels.
  The intended output is a signed provenance record enumerating every
  declassification taken and every flow denied during a run. Kelvra does not
  implement an enforcement engine and does not claim to prevent leakage; it
  claims that the set of points where leakage is possible is finite, declared
  and recorded.
keywords:
  - information flow control
  - AI agents
  - prompt injection
  - privacy
  - audit
license: "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
version: "0.1.0"
